#1 spot channels 1b-1: PSD and PSB fixtures with spot channels, authored by Adobe Photoshop
2025 26.10.0 (scripts/photoshop-probe/spot_psd_take.py, take1, run 20261024T042340Z-dfcc2def;
receipts in ~/devel/doctored-fixtures/photoshop/spot-psd-547/take1).

Each file starts from one of the runner's PNG scenes: S, 32 x 8 opaque, gray v(x) =
round(255 x / 31); St, the same with alpha 0 at x >= 28 (kept as Layer 0; S is flattened to a
Background). 16-bit files are converted to 16 bits BEFORE the spots, CMYK and Grayscale files
converted AFTER them (CnvM, DialogModes.NO). Each spot channel is ONE Make of a new spot channel
(Mk Nw SCch: name, Lab ink, integer solidity), filled from the selection:

  Spot Ramp     Lab (55, 70, 30), from the Red channel loaded as the selection: coverage v(x)
  Spot Bloc é   Lab (80, -20, 60), from the rectangle x in [8, 24), y in [2, 6): full inside

  file         mode, depth   scene   spots (solidity %)
  rgb8.psd     RGB 8         S       Ramp 0, Bloc 100
  rgb8_t.psb   RGB 8         St      Bloc 50 (merged transparency)
  rgb16.psd    RGB 16        S       Ramp 50, Bloc 100
  cmyk8.psd    CMYK 8        S       Ramp 100, Bloc 0
  cmyk16.psb   CMYK 16       S       Ramp 50
  gray8.psd    Gray 8        S       Ramp 100
  gray16.psb   Gray 16       S       Ramp 0, Bloc 50

PSDs were saved with PhotoshopSaveOptions (layers, profile embedded), PSBs through the
largeDocumentFormat save descriptor. Every file reopened in its mode and depth with every spot's
name, kind SPOTCOLOR, solidity and Lab as declared (Photoshop's own DOM readback).

photoshop.json holds, for each file, its sha256, bytes, mode, depth, container, channel count,
merged alpha, first saved plane, the channel resources as hex, and per spot its name, declared
and readback Lab, solidity, DisplayInfo kind and colour space, the stored Lab words and the
stored rows (as the runner's reader reads them).

What the files say, which is the writer's spec (core/src/psd_spot_records.rs):
- a spot channel's plane is stored INVERTED, max - coverage (take1's H1, every file);
- the saved-channel resources are 1006 (Pascal names, Mac Roman, no padding), 1045 (u32 unit
  count including one trailing NUL, UTF-16BE), 1077 (u32 version 1, then 13 bytes a channel:
  colour space 7 = Lab with L, a, b x 100, opacity = solidity, kind 2 = spot) and 1053 (u32
  ids from 3), in that order, and no 1007;
- the first saved plane follows the colour planes and merged alpha; with merged alpha
  (rgb8_t.psb, layer count -1) every list leads with "Transparency" (kind 1, colour space 0,
  65535/0/0/0, opacity 100, id 0), whose plane is the merged alpha;
- the composite is RLE in rgb8, rgb8_t and cmyk8, Raw in the rest.

Read by core/tests/spot_psd_photoshop.rs, which SKIPs when this folder is absent.
